target:    tests/bench/lib/export-snapshot.php
gate:      composer test:export-fidelity
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    strings are stored as BLOB, never TEXT
rationale: Stores string values as SQLITE3_TEXT instead of SQLITE3_BLOB. BLOB is the one SQLite storage class the engine is contractually forbidden to reinterpret; TEXT carries an encoding it may transcode, which is how a 4-byte codepoint or an invalid-UTF-8 sequence stops being the bytes MySQL held. REGISTERED BECAUSE IT ESCAPED FIRST: this mutation originally PASSED the entire cross-language comparison, because the Python reader sets text_factory=bytes and therefore returns TEXT and BLOB identically - the BLOB rule was specified, documented, and proven by nothing. typeof() is where the storage class is decidable, so the gate asserts it there. A guard whose subject the read path cannot observe has to be asserted somewhere the read path is not.
---
diff --git a/tests/bench/lib/export-snapshot.php b/tests/bench/lib/export-snapshot.php
--- a/tests/bench/lib/export-snapshot.php
+++ b/tests/bench/lib/export-snapshot.php
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@
                     } else {
                         // Strings, and integers too wide for SQLite's signed 64-bit INTEGER:
                         // raw bytes, which SQLite must not reinterpret.
-                        $insert->bindValue($i + 1, (string) $value, SQLITE3_BLOB);
+                        $insert->bindValue($i + 1, (string) $value, SQLITE3_TEXT);
                     }
                 }
                 $insert->execute();
